Serve a surface created before any config

GStreamer's va plugin decides at registration whether a driver can export
dma-bufs. It creates a 64x64 NV12 surface with no config and no context,
exports it, and reads the modifier (gst_va_dmabuf_get_modifier_for_format,
1.26.2). Surfaces here take their OUTPUT format from the config's codec,
so with no config there was nothing to set and vaCreateSurfaces failed.
GStreamer then left memory:DMABuf out of every va decoder's caps:

  vah264dec SRC template: video/x-raw(memory:VAMemory), video/x-raw

So vah264dec ! glimagesink negotiated system memory, a CPU copy per frame,
where v4l2slh264dec ! glimagesink negotiates DMABuf (DMA_DRM, NV12) and
is zero-copy.

Serve a surface created before any config from the first decoder that
takes H.264. The probe only asks what layout an exported NV12 surface
has, and any of these decoders answers that with the same linear NV12.
When the real config arrives, its geometry differs and the queues are
renegotiated as for any new geometry (0007/0019).

---
diff --git a/src/surface.c b/src/surface.c
index 85c7af7..57d10c3 100644
--- a/src/surface.c
+++ b/src/surface.c
@@ -213,6 +213,27 @@ VAStatus RequestCreateSurfaces2(VADriverContextP context, unsigned int format,
 	struct object_context *context_object;
 	bool mplane;
 
+	/*
+	 * A surface before any config. GStreamer's va plugin decides at
+	 * registration whether a driver can export dma-bufs by creating a 64x64
+	 * NV12 surface -- no config, no context -- exporting it and reading the
+	 * modifier (gst_va_dmabuf_get_modifier_for_format). With no codec there
+	 * was no OUTPUT format to set, creation failed, and GStreamer offered
+	 * every downstream element system memory only: a CPU copy per frame.
+	 * Serve such a surface from the first decoder that takes H.264; any
+	 * decoder's linear NV12 layout answers the question honestly, and the
+	 * real config later renegotiates the queues as for any new geometry.
+	 */
+	if (pixelformat == 0) {
+		int device = request_find_device(driver_data,
+						 V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE);
+
+		if (device < 0)
+			return VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED;
+		pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE;
+		driver_data->config_device = device;
+	}
+
 	/* Surfaces belong to the decoder the current config chose. */
 	request_use_device(driver_data, driver_data->config_device);
 	mplane = driver_data->devices[driver_data->device].mplane;
